From 3736f2d48072154b2b111d3d4d678c3c95b2b591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:05:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 46/97] ui(win32): switch a non-60-multiple display to a 60 Hz
 multiple while fullscreen

A 60 fps title on a 165 Hz panel cannot pace evenly (2.75 refreshes per
frame); the owner's laptop felt "never locked 60" at 165 Hz and smoother
after setting 60 Hz by hand. display_refresh_match (default true, Windows
only): on fullscreen entry, if the monitor's refresh is not a multiple of
60, pick the highest 60-multiple mode at the same size and depth and apply
it with CDS_FULLSCREEN (Windows restores it at process exit); restored on
fullscreen exit and window close/destroy. Every step is logged
([display-refresh-match]). Not yet run on real hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
